{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הורד", :translit "hurad", :gloss "was brought down"} {:he "ויוסף הורד", :translit "v'yosef hurad", :gloss "and Yosef was brought down"} {:he "הורד שאול", :translit "hurad sha'ul", :gloss "Sha'ul was brought down"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויוסף הורד" "הורד שאול"]}], :frame {:text "The exile of Yosef to Egypt is described with the passive form הורד, 'was brought down,' the same word used when Sha'ul's body was brought down from the walls of Beit Shan (1 Samuel 31:12). The Midrash teaches that Yosef's descent to Egypt and Sha'ul's fall are linked: just as Yosef was tested through his descent, so was Sha'ul. The word הורד conveys that the experience of exile parallels the descent to Gehinnom, as exile is a form of spiritual punishment (Genesis Rabbah 2:4 states that God showed Avraham the Gehinnom beneath the place of the Temple, and the phrase 'they shall go down' in Genesis 37:35 is understood as referring to Gehinnom per Genesis Rabbah 100:3).", :sources ["1 Samuel 31:12" "Genesis 37:35" "Genesis Rabbah 2:4" "Genesis Rabbah 100:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הורידוהו", :translit "horiduhu", :gloss "they brought him down"} {:he "הורידוהו שמה", :translit "horiduhu shammah", :gloss "they brought him down there"} {:he "הורידוהו אלי גבי בנימין", :translit "horiduhu elai gabi binyamin", :gloss "they brought him down to me regarding Benjamin"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הורידוהו שמה" "הורידוהו אלי"]}], :frame {:text "The verse says of Yosef, הורידוהו שמה, 'they brought him down there' to Egypt (Genesis 39:1), using the plural to indicate that Yehudah bore responsibility for Yosef's sale and descent, as Genesis Rabbah 84:16 states that Yehudah initiated the sale of Yosef. Yehudah later pledges to Ya'akov regarding Binyamin, הורידוהו אלי, 'bring him down to me' (Genesis 43:9). Midrash Tanchuma traces measure-for-measure justice: because Yehudah caused Yosef to be brought down, he was compelled to bring Binyamin down as well (Tanchuma, Vayigash 1 links Yehudah's role in the sale to his later responsibility for Binyamin).", :sources ["Genesis 39:1" "Genesis 43:9" "Genesis Rabbah 84:16" "Tanchuma Vayigash 1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויוסף הורד" "הורד שאול"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויוסף הורד", :refs ["Genesis 39:1"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הורד שאול", :refs ["Isaiah 14:11"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הורידוהו שמה" "הורידוהו אלי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הורידוהו שמה", :refs ["Genesis 39:1"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "הורידוהו אלי", :refs ["Genesis 44:21"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:55.740995836Z", :model "glm-5.2"}